article en "Group source archive v1"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons text "The opt-in "
      cons code "nepl3.group-archive"
      cons text " revision 1 root "
      cons code "GroupArchive"
      cons text " contains "
      cons code "sources: nepl3.source-archive/1 SourceSets"
      cons text " and "
      cons code "skeleton: Bytes"
      cons text "."
      nil
    cons " This is a separate descriptor identity; source-set and syntax-archive identities do not change."
    cons " JSON/Rust schema parity and dependency closure are checked by tools."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "The skeleton is structurally checked foundation ForeignClosureGroup data with empty source fields for each provenance and directly traversed syntax bundle."
    cons " One local source set is consumed for every provenance in table order, followed by each entry's syntax bundles in child-first Finish order."
    cons " Empty sets still consume one position."
    cons " Owner/environment/entry order and indices are preserved; only the shared source table and local source memberships are canonicalized."
    cons " Equal content does not merge owners, IDs or revisions."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Each provenance's declarations are restored before its origins/maps are decoded."
    cons " Each bundle's declarations are restored before its node geometry, origins/maps and views are decoded."
    cons " Local stores use metered insertion."
    cons " Missing/extra sets, nonempty skeleton source fields, invalid identities and ownership references reject."
    cons " Encoding validates the original native group; decoding validates the fully reconstructed group before publishing it."
    cons " Neither a different component nor the operation admission ledger supplies a missing local declaration."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "The transport shares typed source-field mechanics with SyntaxArchive."
    cons " It does not rewrite opaque payloads or replace the expanded native v1 component identity."
    cons " Legacy group decoding rejects the archive envelope."
    cons " Standalone closure extraction and existing component digests are evaluated on the reconstructed native group."
    cons " Default Doc integration, general Sentence payload adapters and real-data 4B Work recovery remain separate unfinished work."
    nil
  cons section descriptor "Replaced-field descriptor boundary"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons "Empty skeleton source lists do not establish their element types."
      cons sentence
        cons text " Before encode or decode, SyntaxArchive requires the selected Foundation descriptor to declare SyntaxBundle field 0 as "
        cons code "sources: List(SourceContent)"
        cons text "."
        nil
      cons " GroupArchive also requires ForeignProvenance field 1 to have that exact contract."
      cons sentence
        cons text " Each SourceContent named reference uses package "
        cons code "nepl3.foundation"
        cons text ", revision 1."
        nil
      cons " These checks apply even to empty inputs; an archive deliberately requires its complete replacement contract."
      cons " The selected SchemaRef must match the finalized registry."
      cons " Descriptor lookups and comparisons are charged to the current Budget and respect sticky cancellation."
      cons " These checks supplement full original-native validation, checked skeleton and source-table boundaries, and reconstructed-native validation; they do not change v1 descriptors, wire bytes, or component identities."
      nil
    nil
  cons section compact "Explicit compact component identity v2"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence
        cons text "The opt-in "
        cons code "syntax::group::compact::encode"
        cons text " returns the unchanged GroupArchive transport and a parallel vector of v2 entry digests."
        nil
      cons " Existing encode, decode, FoundationValueCodec, and v1 identity APIs do not implicitly select this path."
      cons " The operation uses one supplied registry, SourceAdmission and Budget."
      cons " It validates the original native group, the replaced-field descriptor contract, the complete empty-source skeleton, each full SourceContent commitment input, and the final archive envelope."
      cons " A failure returns no successful transport/digest pair."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence
        cons text "Let "
        cons code "NDF(v)"
        cons text " mean canonical NDF/1 bytes and "
        cons code "H(d,v)"
        cons text " mean SHA-256 of the literal UTF-8 domain "
        cons code "d"
        cons text " followed by NDF(v)."
        nil
      cons " Each domain below ends in one zero byte."
      nil
    cons list unordered
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "Source commitment: H("
          cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.SourceContent.v2\\0"
          cons text ", full SourceContent)."
          nil
        cons " The record retains the exact Foundation SchemaRef, full SourceRef, URI and text."
        nil nil
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons "A local membership is a List of Bytes32 source commitments, ordered by the existing canonical source ID/revision/digest ordering."
        cons " All declarations remain, including unused ones."
        cons " Empty local sets occupy a position."
        nil nil
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "Provenance: H("
          cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.Provenance.v2\\0"
          cons text ", List(skeleton provenance, List(local membership)))."
          nil
        cons " There is exactly one local set per provenance."
        nil nil
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "Syntax: H("
          cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.Syntax.v2\\0"
          cons text ", List(skeleton ForeignSyntax, List(local memberships)))."
          nil
        cons " Direct foreign bundles contribute in the existing child-first Finish order, followed by their parent bundle."
        cons " Memberships never cross an entry boundary."
        cons " Opaque token payloads are preserved and not traversed."
        nil nil
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "Environment: H("
          cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.Environment.v2\\0"
          cons text ", the encoded environment field)."
          nil
        cons " The owner table index and provenance table reference are excluded here."
        nil nil
      cons item none body cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "Entry: H("
          cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.Entry.v2\\0"
          cons text ", List(Bytes32 provenance commitment, Bytes32 environment commitment, Bytes32 syntax commitment))."
          nil
        cons " References select the appropriate components but their group table indices are not committed."
        nil nil
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "These two-element component envelopes are private hash preimages, not valid stand-alone native syntax or additional transport descriptors."
      cons " Canonical NDF framing and separate domains preserve component and local membership boundaries."
      cons " Components used only by other valid entries do not affect a selected entry identity."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Source commitments are memoized only inside this operation."
      cons " Sorted full SnapshotId lookup is metered; a hit requires exact admitted immutable snapshot equality, including URI and text."
      cons " Independently allocated equal snapshots pay for equality."
      cons " All lookup, insertion shift, component bookkeeping, copies, retained storage, encoded digest input, digest output and transport output consume the same Budget."
      cons " A sticky stop remains a failure on retry."
      cons " No proof or cache crosses operations."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "This Foundation API does not complete default Doc integration, foreign Sentence payload adaptation, or the historical real-data 4B Work acceptance milestone."
      nil
    cons section depths "Consuming-language depths"
    body
      cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons code "compact::encode_at_depths"
          cons text " accepts a typed GroupAtDepths input containing the native group, one occurrence-depth maximum for every entry, and the caller's native registry."
          nil
        cons " This input is not a proof."
        cons " Every call validates the complete input at those depths in the current active Budget depth, before codec boundary work."
        cons " A distinct codec registry receives its own native validation; equivalent registry contents do not authorize skipping this second authority."
        cons " The same private validation helper is used by the existing v1 depth-aware encoding path."
        cons " Missing/extra entry depths and native errors remain GroupEncodingError::Structure; codec registry, archive/schema and encoding failures remain Codec."
        cons " Codec stops are normalized without converting a stopped computation into a partial pair."
        nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "The archive bytes and v2 identities do not include occurrence depths: valid placement changes validation cost and limits, not content identity."
        cons " Depth-aware encoding shares capture and finalization with the ordinary compact operation and does not reconstruct then re-encode the group."
        cons " Archive decoding alone still does not establish the consuming document's occurrence-depth requirements."
        cons " Doc must compute and check its own shared-embed maximum depths after reconstruction."
        nil
      cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "The explicit "
          cons link relative "28-doc-source-archive.md" none text "Doc source archive"
          cons text " consumes this capability without changing existing Doc preparation or rendering identities."
          nil
        nil
      cons paragraph
        cons sentence
          cons text "An identity-only capability is specified separately in "
          cons link relative "32-group-identity-without-transport.md" none text "group commitments without transport"
          cons text "."
          nil
        nil
      nil
    nil
  nil
